Z||000013||Songman||06-20-2001||06:30 PM||||I agree that ME is better than 95, but please if you can get 98SE use it instead.<P>Windows ME is the most resource-hogging operating system I have ever seen.. I used 98SE, ME and 2000 within a month of each other on the same machine. Trust me, go to 98SE unless you have enough computer to go to Windows 2000. 2000 flies!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Robert||06-20-2001||07:17 PM||||Before I upgraded to Windows ME my computer would crap out after 3 days of being on.  Now that I am on ME, I have gone as long as a couple of weeks without rebooting.||||reg||10
Z||000015||Songman||06-20-2001||07:28 PM||||A lot of the rebooting thing is stuff that you have installed that may cause conflicts, more than it is the OS. I run a server from my Windows 2000 machine and it goes forever without rebooting.<P>As always, personal preference will be different for each person. With all of the stuff I do with my computer I consider myself a 'Power User' so Windows 2000 is perfect for me and I wouldn't consider ME. But the tool needs to match the task. ME may work better for somethings. Until I got SP2 for 2000, I couldn't even think of opening a game. Games worked fine with ME when I had it though.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000016||DecadenceR||06-20-2001||07:46 PM||||Win2000 is definitley a good system to use, but from what my friend says his games dont run well on it. So if you're a gamer, then it's not such a good system to use.<BR>I agree, ME hogs resourced. But my grandfather found a program called Tweak that hels with that. I think he got it from Download.com for free, but I'm not totally sure.<BR>And 84Bill, Blows nuts - (adj.) term describing 99% of microsoft products, usually any first run programs. Refers to the way any and all programs have bugs purposely hidden to crash your system at the most in-opportune time. Also means that the program is a total piece of trash.||||reg||1
Z||000017||84Bill||06-20-2001||07:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>I run a server from my Windows 2000 machine and it goes forever without rebooting.<P>As always, personal preference will be different for each person. With all of the stuff I do with my computer I consider myself a 'Power User' so Windows 2000 is perfect for me and I wouldn't consider ME. But the tool needs to match the task. ME may work better for somethings. Until I got SP2 for 2000, I couldn't even think of opening a game. Games worked fine with ME when I had it though.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Windows 2000 from a support standpoint is great!! I also run my home network with Windows 2000 server. The only gripe I have is as with any new(er) OS is the lack of driver support for older periferals and the lack 3d sound support. Others than that 2000 profesional is an excelent OS. It's about time MS got something right.<P>||||reg||14
